; Nested binder forms: the outer `[x]` iterates `[1 2]`; each
; iteration of the outer body re-decodes the inner `(map …)`
; form fresh — including the inner binder vector and inner xs.
; This is the load-bearing case for "binder loops compose under
; cursor replay" on the binary path.
(map [x] [1 2]
  (map [y] [10 20]
    (* x y)))
